{# Lives inside the table's scroll box, under a hairline of its own: the row is
   part of the table, not a control that floats beneath it. It is also the
   table's bottom edge — without it the last row simply falls off — so it is
   drawn whenever there are rows, whether or not there is a page either side of
   this one.

   Stuck to the bottom of that box (`do-pager-sticky`, client/dev-ops.css) and
   opaque against the rows travelling under it: two directions are no use to an
   operator who has to scroll twenty rows to reach them.

   It counts nothing. `20 events` under a page of twenty was a fact about a
   window, and the filter segments above the table now carry the facts about
   the stream — how many are dead-lettered, how many are on Caseworking — so
   the one page-shaped number on the card sat in the smallest type under seven
   dataset-shaped ones and invited them to be read as the same kind of thing.

   Newer and Older, not Previous and Next. The list is newest first and the
   cursor walks it: `direction=backward` from the top of the page reaches the
   events that arrived after these, and `forward` reaches the ones before. An
   operator paging a stream is asking about time, not about the ordinal of a
   page, and `Previous` on a newest-first list points at whichever of the two
   the reader guessed — which is exactly the wrong thing for a control that
   moves a triage window. `rel` still says prev and next, because that is what
   they are to a browser.

   Both directions are always drawn. A footer that renders only the link it has
   moves the other one across the row the moment the first appears, so the
   button an operator is aiming at is somewhere else on the next page; the
   direction there is no page in is a muted span of the same size, in the same
   place. #}
{# Medium, not the button's own weight: they are the quietest controls on the
   card. The muted span wears the same weight, so the unavailable direction is
   the same object, greyed. #}
{% set pagerLink = "btn btn-xs btn-ghost font-medium" %}
{% set pagerDisabled = "btn btn-xs btn-ghost font-medium text-base-content/30" %}
<nav class="do-pager-sticky flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3.5 py-2" aria-label="Pagination" data-testid="do-pager">
  <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2" data-testid="do-pager-links">
    {% if params.previousHref %}
      <a class="{{ pagerLink }}" rel="prev" href="{{ params.previousHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-newer">← Newer</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="{{ pagerDisabled }}" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-newer-disabled">← Newer</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% if params.nextHref %}
      <a class="{{ pagerLink }}" rel="next" href="{{ params.nextHref }}" data-testid="do-pager-older">Older →</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="{{ pagerDisabled }}" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-pager-older-disabled">Older →</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</nav>
